          "**The surgical stress response** activates the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis and sympathetic system: cortisol, catecholamines and glucagon rise, causing **hyperglycaemia, insulin resistance, protein catabolism and lipolysis** - why diabetics destabilise and why carbohydrate loading helps. [Bailey and Love 28e]",
          "**ADH and aldosterone** rise for 2-3 days after surgery, causing **sodium and water retention and oliguria** - post-operative hyponatraemia follows if hypotonic fluids are given. [Bailey and Love 28e]",
