          "**Perioperative myocardial injury** is mainly **type 2 supply-demand mismatch** (tachycardia, hypotension, anaemia, hypoxia) plus some plaque rupture; most is silent - hence troponin surveillance in high-risk patients and continuation of beta-blockers and statins. [ESC 2022]",
